Body:
@Brendonovich Thank you for approving my PR.

Thanks for improving the code. Your https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/18209/commits/1c15cef3de7f3931a7847c362d98b8cb0e4b0cb8 commit made the code more elegant. However, it changed the behavior slightly (`URL.href` adds trailing slash:`new URL("http://localhost:4096").href == "http://localhost:4096/"`). Such trailing slash triggers navigation bugs in consuming code. See the failing tests: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/actions/runs/31237532949/job/93052787926?pr=18209
I've fixed this new issue: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/18209/commits/755fa7c85ab7b697b66b1f0fb6fc274c8189abef

Reproducing on **1.18.15** (npm, Ubuntu 22.04, `opencode web --hostname 0.0.0.0`). Same symptoms: home shows "这里还没有内容 / Nothing here yet", "New session" inert, while `/api/session` returns all sessions correctly.

**Additional finding**: the web frontend bundled in `opencode-ai@1.18.15` is actually the **1.18.14** build (see #41280), so users of 1.18.15 won't see any frontend fix from this PR until the packaging is corrected too.

**Workaround that works** (client-side, no rebuild): seed the bookmark store in localStorage, then reload:

```js
const KEY='opencode.global.dat:server', DIR='/home/your/session/dir';
const st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY)||'{"list":[],"projects":{"local":[]},"lastProject":{},"recentlyClosed":{}}');
st.projects.local.push({worktree:DIR, expanded:true});
st.lastProject={local:DIR};
localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(st));
```

Verified: after reload the session list (grouped by day) and "New session" both work. The same key is what the "Add project" dialog writes when you pick a folder manually.
